      "advisoryBoundary": "A cosmetic retinaldehyde serum, not individualized acne, pigmentation or anti-ageing treatment advice. Retinal is a vitamin A derivative and is not retinol. The manufacturer's 'regular' step is general product positioning, not a personal recommendation to increase strength; use a lower or current strength until tolerated, patch test, introduce gradually at night, avoid the direct eye area, use daytime sunscreen, and stop for persistent burning or irritation. Do not use vitamin A skincare during pregnancy or breastfeeding unless a qualified clinician specifically advises it.",
